### WEBHOOK FLOWS: VERIFIED TRAIT SIGNATURES

`IncomingWebhook` (`crates/types-traits/interfaces/src/connector_types.rs`) is a plain trait
with default methods - you override only what the connector needs. The error type on every
method is `WebhookError`, NOT `IntegrationError`. Argument counts are exact:

```rust
fn get_event_type(
    &self,
    _request: RequestDetails,
) -> Result<EventType, error_stack::Report<WebhookError>>          // ONE arg besides &self

fn get_webhook_event_reference(
    &self,
    _request: RequestDetails,
) -> Result<Option<WebhookResourceReference>, error_stack::Report<WebhookError>>

fn process_payment_webhook(
    &self,
    _request: RequestDetails,
    _connector_webhook_secret: Option<ConnectorWebhookSecrets>,
    _connector_account_details: Option<ConnectorSpecificConfig>,
    _event_context: Option<domain_types::connector_types::EventContext>,
) -> Result<WebhookDetailsResponse, error_stack::Report<WebhookError>>   // FOUR args besides &self

fn verify_webhook_source(
    &self,
    _request: RequestDetails,
    _connector_webhook_secret: Option<ConnectorWebhookSecrets>,
    _connector_account_details: Option<ConnectorSpecificConfig>,
) -> Result<bool, error_stack::Report<WebhookError>>

fn get_webhook_integrity_checks(&self) -> Vec<WebhookIntegrityCheck>
